## v1.1.0

Changes since v1.0.0b4:

+ Add repeated Task execution with bounded Snakemake wildcard rules while retaining one
  impression and one Yuki job.
  - Preserve numeric `stageout/<index>/` layouts in caches, collection, downstream
    aliases, and per-execution logs.
  - Report live subtask progress, retain failed indices in terminal status, and classify
    short executions that fail between polls as runtime failures.
  - Expand nested REANA listings and archive downloads so repeated stageout and logs are
    collected without flattening their directory layout.
+ Register a default local runner on first server start without replacing existing
  runner configuration.
+ Add LHCb release execution through `lb-run`, including nightly slots and the required
  `lhcbdev.cern.ch` CVMFS repository.
  - Treat `lb-run` as a reserved execution environment and validate Task/algorithm
    compatibility before launch.
  - Support dated `lb-conda/PACKAGE/DATE` environments on REANA and reject combining
    `lb-conda` with an `lb_run` declaration.
+ Add export and import of complete immutable impressions through an SSH runner's managed
  store, including transfer routes and background task support. Exclude deposited
  `config.local.json` and staged `lbapi_key.json` credentials in both directions.
+ Harden SSH cached-input Snakefile generation by JSON-encoding shell directives and
  escaping literal braces used by `find -exec`.
+ Inject deposited APD credentials into ordinary and repeated execution Tasks as a
  mode-`0600` `lbapi_key.json` file without exposing the token in commands or logs.
  Preserve the protected local configuration when an impression is deposited again.
+ Preserve REANA cleanup traps while recording subtask status, and collect nested REANA
  results only after every selected file is stored successfully.
+ Fix the development Compose setup so a bind-mounted Celebi checkout is loaded when
  `CELEBI_DIR` is supplied.
+ Set the Yuki package version to `1.1.0`.
